Chapter: RiscvFarStackParam

 Nine parameters and a frame past 2047 bytes: on riscv the ninth is read from
 the stack at an offset one ld cannot encode, so the load must be built from
 lui and add. Each binding reads its predecessor three times so none can be
 folded away. With a = 1 and i = 1000 the answer is 1 + 300 + 1000 = 1301.

Section: Definitions

